SUMMARY:Yayati - Life and Desire
DESCRIPTION:\nHow far will a man go to prolong a life of indulgence? \nThis Kuttiyattam performance interweaves the special pakarnnattam technique with dance to tell the story of Yayati. \nDrawing on the Mahabharata\, the Puranas\, V. S. Khandekar’s celebrated novel\, and Girish Karnad’s play\, the story unfolds as Yayati openly marries Devayani\, daughter of Shukracharya\, preceptor of the Asuras\, and her friend\, the Asura princess Sharmishtha\, in secret. Bound by worldly pleasure\, he goes so far as to borrow his own son’s youth to prolong his indulgence. Will he reckon with the cost of his greed? \n\n\nCredits:\nDirector & Performer: Sooraj Nambiar\nProduction Manager & Coordinator: Aswathy Sarojini\nMizhavu Artistes: Kalamandalam Rajeev & Kalamandalam Vijay\nIdykka: Kalanilayam Unnikrishnan\nMakeup & Chutti: Kalamandalam Vyshak\nTalam: Saritha T. R. \nThis is the tenth edition of the ‘All For Dance’ series presented by Kalavaahini in association with BIC\, curated by Malavika Sarukkai. The ‘All For Dance’ series is presented every quarter at BIC to spotlight some of the best of classical dance from across India. The event is managed by Shreya Nagarajan Singh Arts Development Consultancy. \nIn collaboration with:\n \nVenue: Auditorium\n\n\n\nA Kutiyattam Recital\nPart of the All for Dance Series\nRSVPs closed. Thank you for your interest.\n*Performer*: Sooraj Nambiar\n*Event Categories*: Culture\, Dance\, Heritage\, Performing Arts\, Theatre
URL:https://bangaloreinternationalcentre.org/event/yayati-life-and-desire/
LOCATION:Bangalore International Centre\, 7\, 4th Main Road\, Domlur II Stage\, Bangalore\, Karnataka\, 560071\, India
CATEGORIES:Culture,Dance,Heritage,Performing Arts,Theatre
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://bangaloreinternationalcentre.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/Thumbnail_YLD.jpg
END:VEVENT
