SUMMARY:Decoding Behavioural Insights
DESCRIPTION: \nIncentives and institutions\, culture and power — this panel discussion examines the intersection of behavioural science\, public purpose\, and corporate decision-making in contemporary India\, centred around Sutapa Banerjee’s new book The Business of Business is (Not) Just Business. \nBehavioural economics\, the study of judgement and decision-making\, has a rich academic history and practical applications across nearly every part of human experience. As public policy think tanks and corporate consultancies increasingly adopt and adapt this research\, understanding its core principles has become more important than ever. Drawing on examples from the Indian context\, the panel illustrates the relevance and multidisciplinary reach of behavioural insights in shaping both institutions and everyday decisions. \nVenue: Auditorium\n\n\nHow Behavioural Tools Can Drive Real Change\nRSVP here (https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSckYZQjSwtU2IseIABAZhIBq6f_BIIhX7y245F9qbHW5t1LAA/viewform?usp=publish-editor)\n*Speakers*: Sutapa Banerjee\, Manish Sabharwal\, Prateep Basu\, Sandip Sen\n*Event Categories*: Business
URL:https://bangaloreinternationalcentre.org/event/decoding-behavioural-insights/
LOCATION:Bangalore International Centre\, 7\, 4th Main Road\, Domlur II Stage\, Bangalore\, Karnataka\, 560071\, India
CATEGORIES:Business
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://bangaloreinternationalcentre.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Thumbnail-6.jpg
END:VEVENT
