SUMMARY:Working Girls
DESCRIPTION:133 min | Tamil\, Hindi\, Bangla\, Marathi\, Malayalam and Telugu with English subtitles | 2005 \nInvisible women\, seen through the lens of wit\, humour and dignity. \nDomestic workers\, farmers\, mothers\, ASHA workers\, dancers\, and organisers all labour to sustain society but are rarely acknowledged. Working Girls is a vivid\, genre-defying documentary that traverses India to uncover the invisible yet essential work performed by women. From care work and domestic work to surrogacy and sex work\, the film challenges dominant ideas about labour\, value\, and visibility. \nIt was filmed across the country in Kolkata\, Mumbai\, Shillong\, Latur\, Thiruvananthapuram\, Hyderabad and Madurai. The film is directed by Paromita Vohra and created in collaboration with the Laws of Social Reproduction project. The Laws of Social Reproduction project\, led by Prabha Kotiswaran at King’s College London\, draws on feminist legal theory to study women’s reproductive labour\, and how law renders this labour invisible\, proposing reform toward economic justice for women. \nCredits:\nWriter-Director: Paromita Vohra\nConcept: Prabha Kotiswaran\nCamer: Avijit Mukul Kishore\nEditing: Nishant Radhakrishnan & Sankalp Meshram\nSound: Achuth Sahadevan\, Namshad Hameed\, Rajesh Saseendran\, Sneha Sundar & others\nMusic: Bonnie Chakraborty\nSound Mix: Gissy Michael \nIn collaboration with: \n \nVenue: Auditorium\n\n\nA Witty and Powerful Exploration of Women’s Invisible Labour across India\nRSVP here (https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSfAP_yTAoshSnHLUvRL03B609_nE8Ve5hKWkwVXL__CBqil7Q/viewform?usp=publish-editor)\n*Speakers*: Paromita Vohra\, Anuja Ghosalkar\n*Event Categories*: Film\, Gender\, Society
URL:https://bangaloreinternationalcentre.org/event/working-girls/
LOCATION:Bangalore International Centre\, 7\, 4th Main Road\, Domlur II Stage\, Bangalore\, Karnataka\, 560071\, India
CATEGORIES:Film,Gender,Society
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://bangaloreinternationalcentre.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/Thumbnail_WG.jpg
END:VEVENT
